Add StructureCat and morphism machinery

Introduce a `StructureCat` in `algebra/structure.rs` that bundles a
flat arena of `Structure`s with a set of forward-only element-level
morphisms `(StructureId, StructureId) -> ElMap`.
`StructureCat::close` runs the per-structure saturation in arena
order, pushing `pred_apps`, `func_apps`, `var_els` and
`ambient_model_els` along every outgoing morphism and enqueueing
equalities on the codomain when a pushed entry clashes. It then
walks backward and pulls type information from each codomain back
into the domain for mapped elements whose `ConcreteType` parents are
all ambient model elements (so their preimages in the domain are
unambiguous), re-closing the domain once type info has been imposed.
A final canonicalisation pass rewrites every `ElMap` so keys are
roots in the domain's unification and values are roots in the
codomain's.

`RuleStructures` now stores its structures on a `StructureCat` field
rather than an inline `Vec<Structure>`. `clone_structure` registers
the inclusion as an identity morphism on the source's elements, so
every `If`/`Then`/branch/case/after clone produced by `populate`
ships with a morphism from its predecessor. Branch and match
statements additionally clone a dedicated after-structure (so the
after is a concrete node in the category rather than the reused
predecessor id); the existing TODOs about merging branch/case ends
into the after are preserved.
